    "status": "draft",
    "summary": "rahi reported (its 045 D-22) that a distributed lock left held by a restart strands the next caller until its request times out. This spec records F-138, shows with an end-to-end restart test that the stall is the upstream F-102 behavior `023` B-6 already repaired, and holds the bound the fork gives: the next caller is granted within one lease plus a bounded margin. No source changes.\n",
